{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible","id":1393756,"title":"Dynasty? Is that even possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-03T03:32:08-07:00","id":1393756,"title":"Dynasty? Is that even possible?","content":"My friend run a Fading Suns campaign for a few years, during which we played children and grandchildren of our original characters (in game terms it lasted about 60 years). And I was wondering if it's possible in WoD. I know that Garou has 10% chance for having a Garou children. I read that many Changelings are spouses of Changeling. Gypsie's kids are often Gypsies. I believe that we could rule out dead characters (Wraiths, Cainites, Demons and Mummies). What about Hunters and Mages? Are there any rules for that? And if not how would you calculate the odds for that (except using ST's privileges)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T03:51:16-07:00","id":1393757,"title":"","content":"Don't rule out the Cainites. You could play A who sires B who sires C and so on. That way you can have descendents, even if not strictly biological descendents, and so run a dynastic campaign.<br /> <br /> A problem could be that vampires lives potentially forever. But that can reasonably be avoided by torpor, Final Death if necessary, withdrawing from politics for a more esoteric, or a higher level of politics that makes them not take part in the kind of street-level activites that it seems like many vampires games are about, or other reasons as to why the Sire is not throwing his, or her, weight around like he, or she, used to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T04:04:46-07:00","id":1393758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1393757#post1393757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't rule out the Cainites. You could play A who sires B who sires C and so on. That way you can have descendents, even if not strictly biological descendents, and so run a dynastic campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I ruled out Cainites. They can Embrace anyone and their &quot;children&quot; will always be a Cainite (except maybe Thin Bloods and characters that cannot be Embraced like Hunters, Mummies, Demons, Risen and most shapeshifters). I was thinking about more &quot;human&quot; method of siring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T05:00:14-07:00","id":1393762,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> the thing about the Romani (\u201cGypsies\u201d) is SERIOUSLY racist, but that would absolutely be possible for other splats. Garou and Changeling Powers are definitely inherited. Mage powers don\u2019t technically run in families, but there\u2019s no reason one of your kids couldn\u2019t Awaken too. As for hunters, I guess the Messengers could Imbue the child of a hunter as well.<br /> <br /> Idk about odds. Math is not my thing. Just handwave it, I guess. Your players won\u2019t know or care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:32:33-07:00","id":1393796,"title":"","content":"You could do generational chronicles for all sorts of WoD beings. Very often powers can be hereditary, so it makes sense. I wouldn\u2019t worry about the chances of passing along powers or anything like that. You have an idea, don\u2019t let some background fluff technicality keep you from running the game you want. So what if only 10% of a Garou\u2019s children become Garou themselves, your first characters\u2019 children are in that minority. <br /> <br /> It might actually be interesting to play this in a mixed group with some long lived characters and short lived one. Someone playing a vampire could keep the same character, someone playing a werewolf could change to descendants. \u201cI used to fight side by side with your grandfather just like this.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T10:40:26-07:00","id":1393800,"title":"","content":"While Imbuing and Awakening can happen within a family line, there's no metaphysical aspect to this like there is with werewolves and changelings. When it happens it's a fluke/unique situation (though some mages might try to make it the case).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T11:17:26-07:00","id":1393804,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a descendants game. One work around could be to allow near relatives like nephews and cousins and the like.<br /> <br /> Or don\u2019t worry about having dead characters, because you could always say play characters who became supernatural after starting a family.<br /> <br /> But the Kinfolk/Kinain connection really build off each other. So you could have every character kinfolk and Kinain no matter if they are Mages or Changelings (well if they are Changelings they aren\u2019t Kinain and werewolves aren\u2019t kinfolk but you know what I mean). And if you just had a one off of a Cainite it could work.<br /> <br /> Imagine though the complications if you are a Fallen or Arcadian sidhe, if the family finds out you usurped a soul expect bad blood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T12:10:09-07:00","id":1393815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1393762#post1393762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> the thing about the Romani (\u201cGypsies\u201d) is SERIOUSLY racist, but that would absolutely be possible for other splats. Garou and Changeling Powers are definitely inherited. Mage powers don\u2019t technically run in families, but there\u2019s no reason one of your kids couldn\u2019t Awaken too. As for hunters, I guess the Messengers could Imbue the child of a hunter as well.<br /> <br /> Idk about odds. Math is not my thing. Just handwave it, I guess. Your players won\u2019t know or care.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0lczHvB3Y9s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0lczHvB3Y9s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/0lczHvB3Y9s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/0lczHvB3Y9s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But about the topic, why not instead of Garou just have a Kinfolk Campaign? It is likely that Kinfolk + Kinfolk = Kinfolk with a slight chance of Garou so you can work to build an dynastic empire for Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:11:19-07:00","id":1393833,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I Liked the last paragraph","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T18:54:17-07:00","id":1393896,"title":"","content":"Vampires die. Most Vampires die. IF you take a pair of identical twins who have roughly idendical lives and one is embraced while the other has a natural normal life.. the vampire is more likely to die first.<br /> <br /> That some vampire have survived thousands of years is not the norm, its a show of their wisdom, cunning and ultimately luck.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also the Modern Salubri method too... for those who want to keep everything in the family!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T20:25:11-07:00","id":1393924,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> I love that movie, but I don\u2019t get the connection between that and what I posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T03:23:43-07:00","id":1394009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1393762#post1393762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> the thing about the Romani (\u201cGypsies\u201d) is SERIOUSLY racist, but that would absolutely be possible for other splats. Garou and Changeling Powers are definitely inherited. Mage powers don\u2019t technically run in families, but there\u2019s no reason one of your kids couldn\u2019t Awaken too. As for hunters, I guess the Messengers could Imbue the child of a hunter as well.<br /> <br /> Idk about odds. Math is not my thing. Just handwave it, I guess. Your players won\u2019t know or care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? Racist? When? When I use the word Gypsie or when I wrote about their kids? If the former I used it to clarify about who I'm talking about (sourcebook was called World of Darkness: Gypsies not World of Darkness: Romani). If the latter I was thinking about inheriting powers, not race (and as far as I know they are rather closely knit). I sometimes use racism during my games (I don't like newer, politically correct WoD; racism is part of our world), I know words like n***a, c***k,t*******d etc. Is that make me a racist? Anyway, if you or anyone else was offended then I'm sorry. And what movie you were talking about (in your second post)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-04-2020, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T03:33:22-07:00","id":1394010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1393796#post1393796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do generational chronicles for all sorts of WoD beings. Very often powers can be hereditary, so it makes sense. I wouldn\u2019t worry about the chances of passing along powers or anything like that. You have an idea, don\u2019t let some background fluff technicality keep you from running the game you want. So what if only 10% of a Garou\u2019s children become Garou themselves, your first characters\u2019 children are in that minority. <br /> <br /> It might actually be interesting to play this in a mixed group with some long lived characters and short lived one. Someone playing a vampire could keep the same character, someone playing a werewolf could change to descendants. \u201cI used to fight side by side with your grandfather just like this.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>But that technicalities could actually build the game. Imagine jealousy (&quot;why he is a Garou and not me&quot;), drama (&quot;if he had our powers he could live&quot;) or romance (&quot;I love you, but I am a garou just like you so I have to mate with your brother&quot;). Besides I know that I can use my own rules for that. I was just wandering if there are any rules of inheriting powers for Mages, Changelings etc.<br /> <br /> And I was thinking about a mixed group saga. As I said I was just wondering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T04:11:06-07:00","id":1394014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1393804#post1393804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or don\u2019t worry about having dead characters, because you could always say play characters who became supernatural after starting a family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. Just like in &quot;Queen of the Damned&quot; movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T06:18:30-07:00","id":1394022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394010#post1394010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides I know that I can use my own rules for that. I was just wandering if there are any rules of inheriting powers for Mages</div> </div> </div> </div>While the answer for mages it's <b>no</b> (albeit the Verbena tend to believe otherwise - which in itself could be an interesting factor on a chronicle of the ages), there are artifacts called Primers (usually books, but can be on other formats - like oral tradition) that substantially increase the chances of Awakening. However, there's no system - it requires the user to be &quot;unsually smart and imaginative&quot;, willing to deeply study the work (likely dedicating years) and take the content seriously. Mages who make an effort of training sleepers to awaken may use these as a &quot;last test&quot; of sorts.<br /> <br /> While mage training it's wibbly-wobbly, Sorcerers can be trained. You could easily have a family that has a sorcerous tradition (which also may keep a Premier as a treasure to increase the chances of mages).<br /> <br /> Neither are genetic, but traditions certainly can run in the family - and an old family with an occult tradition can be an interesting background regardless of splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2020, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:47:29-07:00","id":1394067,"title":"","content":"Sorry. Meant to tag <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a>. He sent me a YouTube link and I didn\u2019t get the joke.<br /> <br /> No! I didn\u2019t mean you were racist, I meant the book WoD Gypsies was racist. Although tbh me and my bff once had a fight about that very issue and she agrees with you, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:48:10-07:00","id":1394068,"title":"","content":"Nvm. This is getting off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:24:41-07:00","id":1394095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394067#post1394067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry. Meant to tag <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a>.<br /> <br /> No! I didn\u2019t mean you were racist, I meant the book WoD Gypsies was racist. Although tbh me and my bff once had a fight about that very issue and she agrees with you, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why. But older WoD books had greatest amount of racism, that's true (Swords of Heimdall, Skinhead template etc.). But I also think that makes them more realistic. The newer ones I see as kids: if I close my eyes and don't see anyone/anything then I'm invisible/this thing will dissapear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:16:06-07:00","id":1394108,"title":"","content":"No! I don\u2019t mean racist hate groups portrayed as characters in the setting. I mean the book itself was racist toward the Roma people. I knew this girl whose mom was Romani and she wasn\u2019t anything at all like the stereotypical Gypsy and she definitely didn\u2019t have magical powers.<br /> <br /> Sorry. Like I said, this is way off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:21:39-07:00","id":1394111,"title":"","content":"There was nothing necessarily wrong with the Swords of Heimdall. It's a racist in game faction, not any sort of real world statement. WoD: Gypsies, however, are a real group of people who are being portrayed as semi-human supernatural beings who get magical powers from their racial purity. It was really bizarre. Though, I guess it would be appropriate for a generational game, since the kids of Gypsies are in fact Gypsies too, especially in an alternate universe where a Blood Purity rating exists. Probably best not to follow this tangent anymore though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T12:42:25-07:00","id":1394119,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> agreed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T14:45:59-07:00","id":1394151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394111#post1394111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was nothing necessarily wrong with the Swords of Heimdall. It's a racist in game faction, not any sort of real world statement. WoD: Gypsies, however, are a real group of people who are being portrayed as semi-human supernatural beings who get magical powers from their racial purity. It was really bizarre. Though, I guess it would be appropriate for a generational game, since the kids of Gypsies are in fact Gypsies too, especially in an alternate universe where a Blood Purity rating exists. Probably best not to follow this tangent anymore though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's better way to explain it. I don't know any Romani (besides those who begs on the streets of my hometown, but I doubt they are truly Roma people). The rest of my knowledge about them comes from channels like TLC (I've got two sisters so it was inevitable \ud83d\ude09). Blood Purity may be in fact a little racist but we could say the same about Pure Breed in W:tA. I didn't notice any part of WoD:Gypsies that would describe them as half-humans with powers. Rather humans with powers. But as you said it it's off topic so case closed. I actually like this book. I think that playing humans (even with super powers) in a world infested by werewolves and vampires could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-05-2020, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T06:02:53-07:00","id":1394311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394151#post1394151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Purity may be in fact a little racist but we could say the same about Pure Breed in W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are racists, but for a race that doesn't exist. There are no actual Bonegnawers being harassed in the real life by such misconceptions<br /> <br /> Whereas I can see actual rom being harassed by people that puts weigth in these stereotypes...but that's got nothing to do with you or your table. That the book it's racist doesn't mean that it's racist to play with it, nor with those stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-05-2020, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T07:05:57-07:00","id":1394329,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> true","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:19:44-07:00","id":1394371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible#post1393756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that we could rule out dead characters (Wraiths, Cainites, Demons and Mummies).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this would also depend on time scale you are looking at. Having been in a game that ran through from the pre-imperial Rome to the current day. This was a vampire game, played in several time periods, and with an Werewolf game running along side in the same time periods. The same players all the way through in the main, but playing in the different times, and generailly the &quot;descendants&quot; of those who had gone before.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:55:57-07:00","id":1394396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394151#post1394151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that's better way to explain it. I don't know any Romani (besides those who begs on the streets of my hometown, but I doubt they are truly Roma people). The rest of my knowledge about them comes from channels like TLC (I've got two sisters so it was inevitable \ud83d\ude09). Blood Purity may be in fact a little racist but we could say the same about Pure Breed in W:tA. I didn't notice any part of WoD:Gypsies that would describe them as half-humans with powers. Rather humans with powers. But as you said it it's off topic so case closed. I actually like this book. I think that playing humans (even with super powers) in a world infested by werewolves and vampires could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing inherently racist about blood purity. If there was a breed of dog that had an exceptionally good sense of smell, I suppose you could use role playing rules to represent dogs who have a mixture of that breed, the higher the percentage of that particular dog breed the greater bonus to tracking rolls. That is just one example. I myself have created a WoD style game a creature type based on cambions, humans who have demonic ancestry, which actually has an attribute which is like blood purity and represents how strong the demonic ancestry is and thus how supernaturally powerful (and vulnerable) the cambions are. For some kind of fictional bloodlines, Blood Purity might be fine. If we made a Song of Ice and Fire RPG, maybe a Targaryen could have a Blood Purity score that gave them a bonus to interact with dragons and a bonus to resist fire.<br /> <br /> WoD:G is different than the above examples because Gypsies are a real group of people who do not, in fact, have supernatural powers based on how &quot;pure&quot; their Romani ancestry is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 06-05-2020, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T13:02:06-07:00","id":1394414,"title":"","content":"It all boils down to the fact that Roma people actually exist. I don't think the game developers had malicious intent when they wrote WOD:G, but the problem is that the book is chock full of stereotypes, and reflect racist caricatures, that have been used to justify poor treatment of Roma people that still happens today.<br /> <br /> And there's another factor: Nazis used the idea of eugenics as a justification to murder Roma people on a fairly massive scale. That adds a whole other level of insult to attributing a fictionalized version of the concept to them.<br /> <br /> It's really best to leave that supplement alone and focus more on the truly fictional elements of the setting like Kinfolk, Revenant families, certain Mage bloodlines, or Changelings if you want to explore themes of bloodlines, inheritance, and dynasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:40:20-07:00","id":1394438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394414#post1394414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all boils down to the fact that Roma people actually exist. I don't think the game developers had malicious intent when they wrote WOD:G, but the problem is that the book is chock full of stereotypes, and reflect racist caricatures, that have been used to justify poor treatment of Roma people that still happens today.<br /> <br /> And there's another factor: Nazis used the idea of eugenics as a justification to murder Roma people on a fairly massive scale. That adds a whole other level of insult to attributing a fictionalized version of the concept to them.<br /> <br /> It's really best to leave that supplement alone and focus more on the truly fictional elements of the setting like Kinfolk, Revenant families, certain Mage bloodlines, or Changelings if you want to explore themes of bloodlines, inheritance, and dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>But eugenics is real. It's the genes that makes people from Africa better long distance runners. And, as it may sound cruel, people could be breed like any other animal (and biologically we are animals). As for stereotypes the world is full of them (and they're mostly justified). I've heard polish jokes, I've heard that Poles are drunks and thieves. But we also succeeded where Napoleon and Hitler failed. Twice. I think that any of you could find stereotypes about your race or nationality, either good or bad. But as it was said earlier it's off topic. So maybe we close the discussion about racism and assume that Blood Purity was just a simplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T16:45:45-07:00","id":1394451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394438#post1394438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But eugenics is real. It's the genes that makes people from Africa better long distance runners. And, as it may sound cruel, people could be breed like any other animal (and biologically we are animals). As for stereotypes the world is full of them (and they're mostly justified). I've heard polish jokes, I've heard that Poles are drunks and thieves. But we also succeeded where Napoleon and Hitler failed. Twice. I think that any of you could find stereotypes about your race or nationality, either good or bad. But as it was said earlier it's off topic. So maybe we close the discussion about racism and assume that Blood Purity was just a simplification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, um, okay. Let's change the subject. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that a Revenant game could work well for this. Their powers are passed through the blood and they have enough powers to make them interesting. Another guy and I came up with an alternative setting for V:tM where vampires all disappeared and Revenant families essentially replaced them. We had our own Revenant organizations that were at odds with each other - a group of Revenants who served the Tzimisce and a group that served the Cappadocians, along with independents. A few rule changes too. <br /> <br /> My question would be - what kind of supernatural being interests you the most? Pick something you and your players like and then you can go from there to make your dynasty game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:15:55-07:00","id":1394477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible?p=1394451#post1394451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, um, okay. Let's change the subject. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that a Revenant game could work well for this. Their powers are passed through the blood and they have enough powers to make them interesting. Another guy and I came up with an alternative setting for V:tM where vampires all disappeared and Revenant families essentially replaced them. We had our own Revenant organizations that were at odds with each other - a group of Revenants who served the Tzimisce and a group that served the Cappadocians, along with independents. A few rule changes too. <br /> <br /> My question would be - what kind of supernatural being interests you the most? Pick something you and your players like and then you can go from there to make your dynasty game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I forgot about Revenants. <br /> <br /> My knowledge about WoD menagerie goes like this: Werewolf&gt;Vampire&gt;Mage&gt;Wraith&gt;Changeling&gt;Hunter&gt;Dem on and in between others (Mummies, Revenants, Kuei-jin etc.). So I was thinking mostly about werewolves, using their families (Garou and Kinfolk alike). I like the idea of a Kindred friend of this family. I was also thinking about inheriting the Avatar (The same Avatar &quot;reborn&quot; in a different person) and maybe a little Wraith, but more likely as a background. I have no ideas about the rest, but still I would like to use them as a background too. Most likely I will run a story for a mixed group cause I like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T05:42:22-07:00","id":1394547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1393756-dynasty-is-that-even-possible#post1393756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My friend run a Fading Suns campaign for a few years, during which we played children and grandchildren of our original characters (in game terms it lasted about 60 years). And I was wondering if it's possible in WoD. I know that Garou has 10% chance for having a Garou children. I read that many Changelings are spouses of Changeling. Gypsie's kids are often Gypsies. I believe that we could rule out dead characters (Wraiths, Cainites, Demons and Mummies). What about Hunters and Mages? Are there any rules for that? And if not how would you calculate the odds for that (except using ST's privileges)?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">It should be noted that the term &quot;Gypsy&quot; is a racial slur and the WOD book on them is an Old Shame equivalent to &quot;World of Darkness: Jews&quot; according to Justin Achilli. All of it is non-canon and something that should be avoided being brought up in games, especially the term. You're correct in that this is what the book is called but that's not really helped matters.<br /> <br /> Eugenics is also a debunked pseudo-science that takes the ideas of genetics and misuses them horribly, usually for the purposes of nonsensical racial theories. No reputable scientist considers it anything more than junk science or an Old Shame. Believe me, I know, I worked in academia. Feel free to look this up on free sources like Wikipedia to find out how far from a neutral position this is.<br /> <br /> Between these two, I'm shutting down this thread. Some supernatural groups inherit power via the blood. Most of them who try to breed it like the Tzimisce, fundamentalist Garou, and Progenitors are bad guys. There, you have your answer.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, 